      "platform_excerpts": [
        {
          "issue_slug": "economy",
          "excerpt": "Díaz-Balart voted to promote free trade with Peru, against assisting workers who lose jobs due to globalization, for the Central America Free Trade Agreement, for the US-Australia Free Trade Agreement, for the US-Singapore free trade agreement, and for free trade with Chile.",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "healthcare",
          "excerpt": "On May 4, 2017, Díaz-Balart voted to repeal the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (Obamacare) and pass the American Health Care Act.",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "immigration",
          "excerpt": "In 2026, Díaz-Balart was a cosponsor of the DIGNIDAD Act, which proposes a pathway to legal status for up to 12 million illegal immigrants, paired with stricter border enforcement and mandatory work and restitution requirements.",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "climate",
          "excerpt": "In 2007, Díaz-Balart said, 'My fear is using the bandwagon of global warming to have Congress act on some knee-jerk reaction which will please some editorialists, will hurt our economy, will not do anything to help us in the future.'",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "education",
          "excerpt": "opposes requiring states to adopt federal education standards",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "guns",
          "excerpt": "Díaz-Balart said gun control legislation would not be effective at stopping mass shootings, saying, 'I want to make sure we look at things that could make a difference.'",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "criminal_justice",
          "excerpt": "opposes mandatory minimum sentences for nonviolent drug offenders",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "foreign_policy",
          "excerpt": "Díaz-Balart supported a July 2025 appropriations bill that would ban funding for the United Nations secretariat and UNRWA, saying that the bill 'strengthens national security and supports an America First foreign policy.'",
          "source": "wikipedia",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Diaz-Balart"
        },
        {
          "issue_slug": "taxes",
